### A file over 10 MB is 413 tooLarge on file, and it returns on its own. The file isn't in the repo:
### make it with `head -c 10485761 /dev/zero | tr '\0' a > http-files/over-10-mb.txt`. A request far
### larger than that, over Kestrel's own body limit, gets Kestrel's empty 413 instead.
POST {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards/{{attachmentCard}}/attachments
X-User-Id: {{actorId}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="nope"

Dropped, because tooLarge returns alone
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="over-10-mb.txt"

< ./http-files/over-10-mb.txt
--WebAppBoundary--

