< ./http-files/readme.md
--WebAppBoundary--

> {% client.global.set("attachmentCascade", response.body.data.id); %}

### Archive the card, so it can be deleted. 204.
PUT {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards/{{attachmentCascadeCard}}/archived
X-User-Id: {{actorId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": true
}

### Delete the card. 204, and the foreign key cascades to its attachments, whose rows fire the
### trigger, so the objects go too.
DELETE {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards/{{attachmentCascadeCard}}
X-User-Id: {{actorId}}

### Read the attachment the deleted card held. 404, because the cascade took its row.
GET {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards/{{attachmentCascadeCard}}/attachments/{{attachmentCascade}}

### A card holds at most 100 attachments. The 101st is 409 limitReached with a null field, counted
### before any bytes go to storage. Filling a card by hand takes 100 uploads, so the assertion pass
### covers it and this line records the rule.
GET {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards/{{attachmentCard}}/attachments

### Create the card the link checks use.
POST {{prodigy_board_API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/cards
X-User-Id: {{actorId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Card with links",
  "listId": "{{attachmentList}}",
  "isDueComplete": false
}

